{:edb/db-before-t 2574 :edb/db-after-t 2575 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535887 50 #inst "2026-10-09T09:57:16.720Z" 13194139535887 true] [17592186152155 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372650 13194139535887 true] [17592186152155 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372664 13194139535887 true] [17592186152155 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372670 13194139535887 true] [17592186152155 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372673 13194139535887 true] [17592186152155 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372677 13194139535887 true] [17592186152164 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372657 13194139535887 true] [17592186152164 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372667 13194139535887 true] [17592186152165 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372682 13194139535887 true] [17592186152165 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372685 13194139535887 true] [17592186152165 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372689 13194139535887 true] [17592186310715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372681 13194139535887 true] [17592186372650 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372651 13194139535887 true] [17592186372650 1089 "q-138889" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372650 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535887 true] [17592186372650 1100 "A body of mass $8\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons $(\\text{N}).$\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=4\\sqrt{t}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-3)$ meters per second.\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t=4$ seconds." 13194139535887 true] [17592186372650 1113 #uuid "8c20835d-7bd8-5e9c-8ea5-8bdbf915a1be" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372650 1145 "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-3)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}-\\frac{5}{t-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the acceleration at $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4}}-\\frac{5}{4-3} \\\\  & =1-5 \\\\  & =-4\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the force is\n\n$$\n|F|=|-32|=32\\,\\text{N}.\n$$" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372652 13194139535887 true] [17592186372651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372653 13194139535887 true] [17592186372651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372654 13194139535887 true] [17592186372651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372655 13194139535887 true] [17592186372651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372656 13194139535887 true] [17592186372651 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535887 true] [17592186372651 1041 "selection" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372651 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372655 13194139535887 true] [17592186372651 1110 #uuid "0abc5fc0-d2da-5fa8-8173-bde814c17f00" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372652 1034 "36\\,\\text{N}" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535887 true] [17592186372652 1111 #uuid "f9d5b3d4-64c0-5d57-817a-4225cbe120b8" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372653 1034 "16\\,\\text{N}" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535887 true] [17592186372653 1111 #uuid "efa19a68-6b95-5060-b453-8623e1560f27" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372654 1034 "24\\,\\text{N}" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372654 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535887 true] [17592186372654 1111 #uuid "3c1fc86d-1ed1-5f78-aca6-a90bfedecf2d" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372655 1034 "32\\,\\text{N}" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535887 true] [17592186372655 1111 #uuid "75e68ff6-a34e-58e9-9f7c-c4882bcd1618" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372656 1034 "28\\,\\text{N}" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372656 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535887 true] [17592186372656 1111 #uuid "dcb21bf7-89ea-5846-a793-743ffe5ebf58" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372657 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372658 13194139535887 true] [17592186372657 1089 "q-138900" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372657 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535887 true] [17592186372657 1100 "A body of mass $1.5\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)={t}^{4}-{t}^{3}$ meters.\nFind the expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372657 1113 #uuid "1d0e326c-9947-5e66-959d-db32e939a7f9" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372657 1145 "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =4{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =1.5\\cdot (12{t}^{2}-6t) \\\\  & =18{t}^{2}-9t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372659 13194139535887 true] [17592186372658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372660 13194139535887 true] [17592186372658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372661 13194139535887 true] [17592186372658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372662 13194139535887 true] [17592186372658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372663 13194139535887 true] [17592186372658 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535887 true] [17592186372658 1041 "selection" 13194139535887 true] [17592186372658 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372661 13194139535887 true] [17592186372658 1110 #uuid "efaf7af2-7a96-562f-b508-266989de8149" 13194139